reviews.body:
Thank you for this fix. The bug is still on `main`: the native Bedrock plugin did not get the sampling changes from #2338. `SendStream` still sends `temperature` to every model, so Opus 4.7 and later and the Claude 5 models fail with a 400. `Send` still ignores `--temperature`.

The PR cannot merge in its current form. Please make these changes.

### 1. Rebase onto `main`

#2338 (the Anthropic SDK v2 upgrade) removed `anthropic.ModelDisallowsSamplingParams`. The PR calls it, so the branch does not compile on `main`. The CI checks passed before #2338 merged, so they do not show this.

The current function is `ModelAcceptsSamplingParams` in `internal/plugins/ai/anthropic/anthropic.go`. It is an allowlist of the older Claude models that accept `temperature` and `top_p`.

### 2. Do not change non-Claude models

The Bedrock plugin also sends requests to Nova, Llama, Mistral, and other models. `ModelAcceptsSamplingParams` returns false for all of them. A direct change to `!ModelAcceptsSamplingParams(opts.Model)` removes `temperature` from those models too.

Apply the allowlist to Claude models only:

```go
// inferenceConfig returns the sampling settings for a Converse or ConverseStream request.
// Claude models reject a request that sets both temperature and top_p, so the request
// sends temperature only. Newer Claude models reject all sampling parameters and get none.
func inferenceConfig(opts *domain.ChatOptions) *types.InferenceConfiguration {
	if strings.Contains(opts.Model, "anthropic.claude") && !anthropicplugin.ModelAcceptsSamplingParams(opts.Model) {
		return nil
	}
	return &types.InferenceConfiguration{
		Temperature: aws.Float32(float32(opts.Temperature)),
	}
}
```

The `anthropic.claude` substring matches the base IDs and the `us.`, `eu.`, `ap.`, and `global.` inference profile IDs.

### 3. Add a test for a non-Claude model

Add a non-Claude model to `TestSampling_KeptForOtherModels`, for example `us.meta.llama3-3-70b-instruct-v1:0` or `us.amazon.nova-pro-v1:0`. This test fails if a later change removes `temperature` from non-Claude models.

```go
for _, model := range []string{
	"anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929-v1:0",
	"us.amazon.nova-pro-v1:0",
} {
	config := inferenceConfigOf(t, sendOnce(t, stream, model))
	assert.InDelta(t, 0.7, config["temperature"], 0.001, "stream=%v model=%s", stream, model)
}
```

The other parts of the PR are good: the one helper for both send paths, and the tests against a local server. After these changes, I will review it again.
